window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>She saw something she shouldn't. Now the monsters see her.</b></p> <p>In the hidden world beneath modern Boston, power is currency—and blood is never just blood. <i>Shadow Bound</i> is a dark, slow-burn urban fantasy about dangerous alliances, buried truths, and the thin line between hunter and prey. With sharp dialogue, layered politics, and a supernatural mystery at its core, this is a story where no one is safe, nothing is as it seems, and survival means choosing who to trust before the shadows close in.</p> <p>Madison Callahan doesn't believe in monsters. She manages a Boston tanning salon, juggles rent and bad memories, and tries not to think about the ex who left her hollow. Life is predictable, practical—until a strange customer vanishes mid-session and leaves behind nothing but ash. That night, Maddie's routine cracks open. Her only mistake? Asking questions. Now something ancient and dangerous has noticed her—and it won't look away.</p> <p>Gideon Blackwell has seen centuries of war. As a vampire Elder, Gideon walks the tightrope of supernatural politics, managing factions, finances, and the rising threat of a rival who wants his seat of power. But when a low-level vampire vanishes under impossible circumstances, Gideon is forced to investigate the one thing that still terrifies his kind: the unknown. What he finds at a rundown Boston salon shouldn't be possible. And yet, it changes everything.</p> <p>A human caught in the dark. A vampire chasing the truth. Maddie and Gideon were never supposed to meet. But when a single mystery ties their fates together, they'll uncover secrets buried deep in the bones of the city—and in themselves. Because in a world where shadows hide ancient enemies, survival depends on trust, and the line between human and monster is thinner than anyone dares to admit.</p> <p>Warnings: Violence, Mental/emotional distress, Death, Kidnapping, Psychological abuse, Existential horror, Romantic &amp; sexual tension, Strong language &amp; sarcasm</p>"; 
